			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#94">I owe you an explaination</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							As some of you know, I left the guild last night. I would like to explain the reasons for doing so. There are 2 reasons, but i'll start with the main one. I have been invited into several guilds in the last week or so. One of them is very large, and high lvl. Lately, I have been fighting in some of the higher lvl areas like velious, Trakanon's teeth, city of mist, and have been grouping with lvl 45-55 players. I am learning the value of teamwork, and communication within a grp, and within a guild. My needs as a lvl 40 cannot be met without the assistance of other high lvl players. It's hard to participate in large raids when your not in the guild that's doing the raid. I have done some, but it's not easy. The fact is that this is a lower lvl guild, and caters to the lower lvl player. That is a great thing, and alot can be learned in this guild, but I am at the point where I need to move on to higher lvl and more experienced guilds. I really had to think this through because the thought of leaving you all was upsetting. Now comes reason#2. I have to be honest about this, I was dissapointed in what Happened at today's event in the arena. Here's the short version: I travelled from the far side of velious to participate in the meeting, and the event. a trip that was not easy by any means. I saw people screwing off in the meeting, causing Rosy to get irate. Next, i see people getting pissed off because of the way others chose to fight in a PVP arena. third, I see two people put in charge of the event after Rosy leaves. One is not a member of the guild, and neither are even officers. and lastly, The few of us that are lvl 35+ did not get a chance to participate in our own event. I mentioned it several times, but was ignored by the people &quot;in charge.&quot; I spent over 4 hours waiting, and never got an opportunity. I made up my mind at that point to disband. These are only my opinions, and are not meant to discourage others. I was mad when I left, but I also remember all of the good times and great friends I have made in the 8 months I have been a RAGER. I wish to maintain my friendships, and will always offer my help to a rager. I will miss each of you, and don't hesitate to say hello, or help when I'm nearby. Just one more note to add... If I were asked who might fill my shoes as an elder, I would consider Batu my first choice. He was maimed by verant, but remained resilient, and strong. He has come back with a vengeance, and a great attitude.<br />
<br />
Take care all.<br />
Shidosan
						</td>
					</tr>
